backups/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Things that are deliberately NOT committed
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Drafts, scratch files, anything half-finished. Put it in `_private/` and it
# cannot reach a commit by accident.
#
# Why: on 2026-09-16 a `git add -A` swept two untracked working files into
# commits on public repositories. They came out of HEAD in minutes; the commits
# are still in the history, and taking them out means a force-push.
#
# The rule that goes with the folder: stage files by NAME. Never `git add -A`.
_private/
